Japanese TV Standard "ARIB STD-B25" implementation without B-CAS Card
You can use this code for your TV product.

In addition:
If you have plan to design TV hardware product, you can embed bcasid.inf into firmware, because bcasid.inf is fixed value.

Usage:

Install the PC/SC development headers and library required by `bcasid` first.
On AlmaLinux: `sudo dnf install pcsc-lite-devel`. On Debian or Ubuntu:
`sudo apt install libpcsclite-dev`.

Running `bcasid` additionally requires the PC/SC daemon (pcscd), a smart card
reader driver, and a B-CAS card inserted in a connected reader.
On AlmaLinux:

sudo dnf install pcsc-lite pcsc-lite-ccid
sudo systemctl enable --now pcscd.socket

On Debian or Ubuntu: `sudo apt install pcscd`.

make
sudo make install

To generate `/etc/bcasid.inf` from a connected B-CAS card, run:

sudo make bcasid-inf

Set `BCASID_INFO=/path/to/file` to write the generated information to a
different path. Set `PREFIX=/path/to/prefix` to install somewhere other than
`/usr/local`.

Have fun! 
I expect succsess of your business in Japan.
